course: dictionary
lesson: 5123
title: One word, different meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Some words change their meaning with the sentence around them. Invalid is one of these. Look at the clues before you decide what it means. «The UN General Assembly called the referendum invalid.» The clue is that the UN is judging a vote, so invalid must mean not legally acceptable.
explain: Computers and maths use invalid too. If you type a letter where a number should go, the computer may say «invalid input». That means it cannot use what you typed. Ask yourself: does the answer follow the rules? If not, it is invalid.
explain: Invalid also has an old, hurtful meaning for a person who is ill for a long time. You may meet it in old stories, where «an invalid lies in bed». Today that use is old-fashioned and can hurt people, so do not use it about a person. Say someone is ill or has a long-term illness instead.
fact: Invalid is an adjective when it means not acceptable or not correct, and it is said in-VAL-id.
fact: Invalid means not legally or officially acceptable, like an invalid ticket.
fact: Invalid also means not correct or not based on good reasons, like an invalid argument.
fact: «Invalid input» means a computer cannot use what you typed.
fact: As a noun, an invalid (said IN-va-lid) means a person who is ill or disabled for a long time; this use is old and can be hurtful, so avoid it.
exercise: «The UN General Assembly called the referendum invalid.» What does invalid mean here? | *Not legally acceptable | Very big and important | Very old | Happy and bright
exercise: Your computer says «invalid input» when you type a letter where a number should go. What does this mean? | The computer is broken for ever | *The computer cannot use what you typed | You typed the right answer | The computer is tired and needs sleep
exercise: In an old story, «an invalid lies in bed all day». What does invalid mean here? | A ticket that is not accepted | A wrong answer in a sum | *A person who has been ill for a long time | A small boat on a river
test: Your bus ticket has expired, so it is ... | Correct | Valid | Lucky | *Invalid
test: Which word means the same as not based on good reasons? | Strong | *Invalid | Bright | Kind
exam: How is the adjective invalid said? | in-VAL-lid | in-va-LEED | *in-VAL-id | IN-va-lid
